From: liviyifan <344781483+liviyifan@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] block: fitblk: add compat_ioctl

fitblk only sets .ioctl. A compat task (AArch32, or AArch64 ILP32) calls
ioctl() through compat_sys_ioctl() -> compat_blkdev_ioctl(), which returns
-ENOIOCTLCMD (ENOTTY to user space) when the driver has no compat_ioctl.
So "fitblk /dev/fit0" (FITBLK_RELEASE) fails in sysupgrade stage2 of a
compat user space, ubiblock cannot remove the busy volume and the upgrade
aborts before writing anything.

FITBLK_RELEASE takes no argument, so blkdev_compat_ptr_ioctl() is enough.

Signed-off-by: liviyifan <344781483+liviyifan@users.noreply.github.com>
---
--- a/drivers/block/fitblk.c
+++ b/drivers/block/fitblk.c
@@ -183,6 +183,7 @@ static int fitblk_ioctl(struct block_dev
 static const struct block_device_operations fitblk_fops = {
 	.owner		= THIS_MODULE,
 	.ioctl		= fitblk_ioctl,
+	.compat_ioctl	= blkdev_compat_ptr_ioctl,
 	.open		= fitblk_open,
 	.release	= fitblk_release,
 	.submit_bio	= fitblk_submit_bio,
